 {:name "count-preservation / corrupt-one-key mutation check for aggregations"
  :how "Two-part mechanical check. (1) Static: find every aggregation site — grep for (keep ..., (filter ... with a when-let/nil-returning predicate, reduce +/max over keeps, and Python 'for x in pop: if not lookup(x): continue' — and require each site to have a sibling census artifact (a dropped-items list that is refused-on-nonempty or printed by name, like gen_rnode_dossiers' `unjoined`). Flag any keep/filter/reduce-over-lookup whose input population has no such census. (2) Dynamic, the stronger half: a mutation harness that takes each generator/reporter's INPUT fixture, corrupts exactly one lookup key (rename one :track-id, one c_joint, one :evidence/at, one union declaration name), reruns, and diffs the output. PASS = output refuses or the diff names the dropped item explicitly. FAIL = output renders valid EDN/PDF with every number present and exactly one item silently missing — that is this defect class, mechanically detected."
  :false-positive-risk "Legitimate population splits: code that intentionally partitions a population (e.g. gen_model_coverage's 'unclassified' area is rendered and separately counted, rung_claims' blocked message IS the census for its rung) looks like a silent drop to the static grep. The dynamic harness avoids this only if the checker knows which output line is the census; where a drop is reported elsewhere in the same artifact, the static check must trace the census variable, not just its presence."}}
